[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Flying Cats]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.70]Lesson 9 | 第9课
[00:02.62]Flying cats | 飞猫
[00:10.02]How do cats try to protect themselves when falling from great heights? | 猫从高处掉下来时如何设法保护自己？
[00:17.34]Cats never fail to fascinate human beings. | 猫总能引起人们极大的兴趣。
[00:21.77]They can be friendly and affectionate towards humans, but they lead mysterious lives of their own as well. | 它们可以对人友好、充满柔情，但同时也过着神秘的自我生活。
[00:29.47]They never become submissive like dogs and horses. | 它们从不变得像狗和马那样顺从。
[00:33.63]As a result, humans have learned to respect feline independence. | 结果是，人类学会了尊重猫的独立个性。
[00:39.36]Most cats remain suspicious of humans all their lives. | 大多数猫一生都对人类心存戒备。
[00:43.91]One of the things that fascinates us most about cats is the popular belief that they have nine lives. | 最使我们感兴趣的事情之一，就是人们普遍相信猫有九条命。
[00:51.86]Apparently, there is a good deal of truth in this idea. | 显然，这种说法颇有道理。
[00:57.69]A cat's ability to survive falls is based on fact. | 猫在跌落时能够存活下来，这是有事实依据的。
[01:03.18]Recently the New York Animal Medical Centre made a study of 132 cats over a period of five months. | 最近，纽约动物医疗中心对132只猫进行了为期5个月的研究。
[01:13.00]All these cats had one experience in common: they had fallen off high buildings, | 所有这些猫都有一个共同的经历：都曾从高楼坠下，
[01:17.88]yet only eight of them died from shock or injuries. | 却只有8只因休克或受伤而死。
[01:24.07]Of course, New York is the ideal place for such an interesting study, because there is no shortage of tall buildings. | 当然，纽约是进行这项有趣研究的理想之地，因为那里不缺高楼大厦。
[01:33.79]There are plenty of high-rise windowsills to fall from! | 有的是可供坠落的高层窗台！
[01:38.48]One cat, Sabrina, fell 32 storeys, yet only suffered from a broken tooth. | 有一只叫萨布丽娜的猫从32层楼上坠落，却只摔断了一颗牙。
[01:46.89]'Cats behave like well-trained paratroopers,' a doctor said. | “猫就像训练有素的跳伞队员，”一位医生说。
[01:52.15]It seems that the further cats fall, the less they are likely to injure themselves. | 看起来，猫跌落的距离越长，就越不容易伤着自己。
[01:59.16]In a long drop, they reach speeds of 60 miles an hour and more. | 在长距离坠落中，它们的时速可达60英里甚至更快。
[02:05.01]At high speeds, falling cats have time to relax. | 在高速下坠时，猫有时间放松身体。
[02:09.23]They stretch out their legs like flying squirrels. | 它们像飞松鼠一样伸展四肢。
[02:13.69]This increases their air-resistance and reduces the shock of impact when they hit the ground. | 这就加大了空气阻力，并减小了它们着地时的冲击力。
